# CLIENT desktop (laptop/chromebook/desktop) ONLY — copied into the sysroot by
# build-x86-host-stage4.sh solely for ROLE_CLIENT (nodes don't run X). The complete
# set of USE changes the desktop payload needs, from `emerge --pretend --autounmask`
# replayed against the build sysroot:
#   freetype[harfbuzz] — the GTK3 stack (pango → openbox/lxpanel/lightdm-gtk-greeter)
#   libdom[xml]        — www-client/netsurf (svgtiny/svg)
#   nftables[...]      — net-firewall/firewalld backend (FD-06 shields-up)
#   discover[flatpak]  — the desktop-app-governance store backend (FD-09 inc 7 /
#                        admin-bff #115): builds Discover's Flatpak backend so the
#                        provision_desktop_governance() Flatpak-remote config has a
#                        backend to drive; pulls sys-apps/flatpak. Other backends
#                        (snap/firmware/webengine) left OFF — the governed store is
#                        Flatpak-over-OCI only. (Discover's Qt6/KF6 deps are
#                        Qt6-native packages, NOT gated by the make.conf -qt6, so
#                        no qt USE override is needed here.)
media-libs/freetype harfbuzz
net-libs/libdom xml
# libdbusmenu[gtk3] — xfce-base/xfce4-panel[dbusmenu] (via xfce4-meta, the
# 'full'/XFCE desktop weight) hard-requires >=dev-libs/libdbusmenu-16.04.0[gtk3].
# This entry previously lived ONLY in package.use/capable, which the builder
# copies solely for the CAPABLE (Plasma) set — so the plain XFCE desktop role
# walled at resolution (2026-08-15 fleet run, build-desktop.x86.log; issue #60
# item 1). It belongs here: 'desktop' is copied for EVERY client role, and an
# entry for a package a given weight doesn't pull is simply ignored by portage.
dev-libs/libdbusmenu gtk3
# Same move (capable -> desktop), same chain class: xfce4-meta -> thunar-volman
# hard-requires thunar[udisks] -> gvfs[udisks] on the plain XFCE weight too
# (proved by replaying the payload resolution against the failed 08-15 sysroot
# in hugmesh-builder — rc=0 only with these three; udisks is not in the global
# desktop USE, so they must be per-package).
xfce-base/thunar udisks
gnome-base/gvfs udisks
net-firewall/nftables python json xtables
# 'x11-libs/libdrm video_cards_radeon' USED to sit here, for the xf86-video-ati DDX
# that x11-base/xorg-drivers pulls. Removed: it was redundant when it mattered and a
# lie when it did not. libdrm has a video_cards_* IUSE, so it INHERITS make.conf's
# VIDEO_CARDS — which carries 'radeon' exactly for --gpu-driver amd-free, the only
# selection under which xorg-drivers pulls xf86-video-ati at all. Under every other
# --gpu-driver the pin claimed a card the image does not have, which is the same
# class of spec/argv disagreement that killed the 2026-08-22 edge_ai build via
# package.use/gpu. No video_cards_* token belongs in package.use — see that file.
kde-plasma/discover flatpak
# Discover's Qt6/appstream stack tightened in newer releases (the note above is now
# stale): the AppStream backend needs qt6, xdg-utils' man pages need xmlto[text], and
# qtmultimedia (pulled via the KF6/Qt6 multimedia libs) has REQUIRED_USE
# "vaapi? ( opengl )" — vaapi is on from the GPU profile, so opengl must be too.
# These apply to BOTH thin and thick (both ship Discover), hence desktop not capable.
dev-libs/appstream qt6
app-text/xmlto text
# boost[python] moved to package.use/boost (calamares is not client-only).
# Rest of the calamares payload USE closure, computed by converging the SAME
# resolution the builder runs (chroot pretend loop against the live sysroot,
# 2026-07-08) until it succeeded — the failure surfaces only ONE package per
# build cycle otherwise ("--autounmask-continue is NOT applying needed USE
# changes in this chroot", see the payload-emerge diagnostic in
# build-x86-host-stage4.sh):
#   libpwquality[python] — direct calamares dep (password quality page)
#   grub[mount]          — calamares → sys-boot/os-prober needs grub-mount
#   libcanberra[alsa]    — calamares → KF6 knotifications → libcanberra, whose
#                          REQUIRED_USE 'udev? ( alsa )' trips because udev is
#                          on globally; alsa (not -udev) is right for a desktop
dev-libs/libpwquality python
sys-boot/grub mount
media-libs/libcanberra alsa
# Discover is a Qt6/QML Plasma app: it pulls purpose -> prison[qml] and the wider
# KF6/Qt6 QML framework stack. These modules USE-match qtbase[opengl=,vulkan=] and
# need qml, so enable opengl/vulkan/qml across the chain. qtbase also needs
# libproxy/icu/wayland for the Plasma libs. Shared by thin AND thick (both ship
# Discover); thick's capable file only ADDS the heavier app-specific flags on top.
# (Entries for modules a given weight doesn't pull are simply ignored by portage.)
dev-qt/qtbase opengl libproxy icu wayland
dev-qt/qtmultimedia qml opengl
dev-qt/qttools opengl
dev-qt/qtdeclarative opengl vulkan
dev-qt/qtquick3d opengl vulkan
dev-qt/qt5compat qml icu
kde-frameworks/prison qml
kde-frameworks/kconfig qml
kde-frameworks/sonnet qml
media-libs/mesa wayland
sys-libs/zlib minizip
x11-libs/gtk+ wayland
